[results]
The provided section headings report that intrathecal AAV delivery reached DRG neurons without infecting spinal cord dorsal horn neurons, that AAV2/5-shRNA-Nav1.3 reduced Nav1.3 mRNA expression in lumbar DRGs, that Nav1.3 knockdown reduced nociceptive hyperexcitability associated with diabetic neuropathic pain, and that Nav1.3 knockdown in DRG neurons reduced neuropathic tactile allodynia in diabetic rats. No specific quantitative values, effect sizes, p-values, or sample sizes are available in the supplied excerpt.
[context]
Key conditions included streptozotocin-induced diabetes in rats, intrathecal AAV2/5 injection, lumbar DRG as the primary transduced tissue, and assessment of pain behavior and electrophysiological hyperexcitability. The paper does not provide details on vector dose, injection coordinates, animal numbers, behavioral test parameters, or statistical thresholds in the supplied excerpt. It also does not include dentate gyrus stereotaxic injection, S1PR1 manipulation, memory testing, or pharmacological S1PR1 agonist treatment, so its relevance is limited to the AAV shRNA knockdown and pain-behavior component of the proposed plan.
