[method]
The paper used Golgi staining followed by dendritic spine analysis in spinal dorsal horn neurons from rats subjected to spinal nerve ligation (SNL), electroacupuncture (EA), and CN04 treatment. This morphological approach is directly analogous to the proposed Golgi staining component for assessing dendritic complexity, total dendritic length, and spine morphology, although the paper examined spinal dorsal horn neurons rather than hippocampal dentate gyrus neurons and did not use transmission electron microscopy to quantify excitatory synapses or postsynaptic density dimensions.
