[context]
The experiments were performed in a rat SNL neuropathic pain model with EA stimulation and CN04 intervention. Golgi staining was applied to spinal dorsal horn neurons for dendritic spine analysis, and the morphological findings were interpreted alongside behavioral pain thresholds and molecular readouts such as Rac1 activity, p-NR2B expression, PSD95 expression, and the F-actin/G-actin ratio. This context is relevant to the proposed research plan because it demonstrates Golgi-based assessment of structural spine plasticity in a chronic pain model, but it differs from the proposed mouse CCI model, dentate gyrus region, and TEM-based quantification of excitatory synapses and postsynaptic densities.
