Processing method: To investigate actin cytoskeleton regulation and S1PR1 protein interactions: We will examine actin cytoskeleton regulation by measuring F-actin/G-actin ratios and analyzing expression of key regulatory proteins (Rac1, Cdc42, Arp2/3, ITGA2). Yeast two-hybrid screening will be used to identify potential S1PR1 protein interactions, with co-immunoprecipitation assays to validate interactions in mouse DG tissue.
Processing method: To examine structural plasticity changes: Using TEM, we will quantify the number of excitatory synapses per unit area and measure postsynaptic density dimensions in the DG. Golgi staining will be used to analyze dendritic complexity, total dendritic length, and spine morphology (mushroom/stubby vs. thin/filopodia types).
Processing method: To validate RNA-sequencing findings: Western blotting will be used to validate key protein expression changes, particularly S1PR1 and downstream signaling molecules.
Processing method: To test the causal role of S1PR1 in the DG: We will generate AAV vectors for S1PR1 knockdown (shRNA) and overexpression, delivering them bilaterally into the DG via stereotaxic injection. Control groups will receive scrambled shRNA vectors. We will assess the effects on pain sensitivity and memory performance using the same behavioral paradigms.
Processing method: To validate S1PR1 signaling pharmacologically: We will implant cannulas into the DG and deliver the S1PR1 agonist SEW2871 continuously for 14 days starting from day 7 post-CCI. We will evaluate effects on S1PR1 expression, pain thresholds, and memory performance.
Processing method: To identify molecular mechanisms underlying susceptibility, with emphasis on sphingolipid metabolism and S1P signaling: We will perform RNA-sequencing on DG tissue from Sham, susceptible, and unsusceptible mice at 28 days post-CCI to identify differentially expressed genes and enriched pathways.
Processing method: To characterize pain and memory phenotypes: We will conduct chronic constrictive injury surgery on mice and assess pain thresholds using von Frey filaments (mechanical allodynia) and Hargreaves test (thermal hyperalgesia). Spatial memory will be evaluated using Y-maze test and Morris water maze (MWM) at multiple time points post-injury.
Processing method: To segregate susceptible and unsusceptible phenotypes: We will use k-means clustering (k=2) to segregate mice into susceptible and unsusceptible populations based on memory performance cutoff values.
